ation method for brain mapping</article-title><source><italic>Medical Image Analysis</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>7</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>130</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12868617</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Qi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Shen</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Learning-based deformable registration of MR brain images</article-title><source><italic>IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>25</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>1145</fpage><lpage>1157</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16967800</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glocker</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Komodakis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Paragios</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Tziritas</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Navab</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inter and intramodal deformable registration: continuous deformations meet efficient optimal linear programming</article-title><conf-name>In: Proceedings of the Information Processing in Medical Imaging (IPMI '07)</conf-name><conf-date>July 2007</conf-date><conf-loc>Kerkrade, The Netherlands</conf-loc></element-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ashburner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A fast diffeomorphic  image registration algorithm</article-title><source><italic>NeuroImage</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>38</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>113</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17761438</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rohr</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Stiehl</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Sprengel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Buzug</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Weese</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuhn</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Landmark-based elastic registration using approximating thin-plate splines</article-title><source><italic>IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>20</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>526</fpage><lpage>534</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11437112</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pelizzari</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>GT</given-names></name><name><surname>Spelbring</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Weichselbaum</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Accurate three dimensional registration of ct, pet, and/or mr images of the brain</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Computer Assisted Tomography</italic></source><year>1989</year><volume>13</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>20</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2492038</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Besl<